      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (often given as 850 mg TID). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nCould this be a transposition or a total-daily-dose mix-up? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg BID.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO BID or TID**, a more typical regimen.\n\nIf you do want 1700 mg TID, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
